-- title:
--   Supersingular chart has q+1 ends permuted by level automorphisms (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 3$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ not divisible by $q$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the intermediate field $\kappa(j_q, j_{q,M'}) \subseteq \kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by the $j$-series `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold expansion `jqNModC`, whose members are exactly the supersingular places: the rational places that are affine geometric and whose value on `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`; let $s$ be one of them. Assume the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ for the kernel $H$ of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Further data: intermediate fields $\mathbb Q \subseteq k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $k_0 \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ that is the contraction of $A$, an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$; a $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ for which the Drinfeld coordinate ring `CoordRing q κ` (two variables modulo `drinfeldPoly` $-\,1$) is a domain; a subring $B \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` that is an $A_b$-algebra and is stable under every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ together with a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` with residue field $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` contracting to $A$, with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$, and such that every nonzero element can be scaled into the integers with nonzero residue), with $B \subseteq$ `R.integers`; a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$; a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field `quotField q κ Cs` of the associated subgroup of automorphisms of the Drinfeld function field, whose image consists exactly of those elements of that fixed field coming from `CoordRing q κ`; and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : F_{ss} \to$ `quotField q κ Cs` with $e$ of the residue of $b$ equal to $\rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$. Under these hypotheses there is a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ with exactly $q + 1$ elements such that a place $Q$ fails to lie in $N$ precisely when the residue of every element of $B$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and such that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) which preserves `R.integers`, the induced automorphism `R.resAut` of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ permutes $N$: one has $\tau \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$.
--
--   This is the count of the ends (the points at infinity) of the supersingular component of the semistable reduction read off an affine chart, in the case $q = 3$: after identifying the reduced function field with the $C_s$-invariants of the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$, the places where the chart degenerates number $q+1$ and are permuted by the level automorphisms. It feeds the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and the base smooth point stalks at level $q = 3$.
